Metadata transfer import rejects remote peering routes
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/49d3fbec5a2c8191bfb79f00577762fd?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: informational (attack path: ignore)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`9123ccc6`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/9123ccc6) (`Add metadata PG transfer and backfill UAT coverage`).

The finding was valid for the reported commit `78b6e3a`: remote metadata-transfer destination validation selected Peering PG routes, but the Unix/RPC server handlers for `MetadataCommandReplicaStateCanInitialize` and replay-state validation still used the Active-only `validate_pg_route` helper.

The fix changed those metadata peering inspection RPC handlers to use `validate_pg_route_for_peering_inspection`, which permits current-epoch `Active` and `Peering` routes and supports retained historical Peering route inspection where required. The current code therefore allows remote/multihost metadata transfer import to validate empty and already-imported Peering destinations instead of failing with `InactivePgRoute`.

Regression coverage now includes `storage_node_server_allows_peering_metadata_transfer_destination_checks`, which exercises `MetadataCommandReplicaStateCanInitialize` against a Peering route, and `storage_node_server_allows_peering_metadata_transfer_adopt_and_validate`, which validates the replay-state path under a Peering destination route.

Verification for the resolution:
- `cargo test -p storage metadata_transfer_destination_checks -- --nocapture`
- `cargo nextest run` on commit `867d9813` passed 5576 tests.

