## Report
Validated the finding as a real availability/operational bug in the Unix/RPC-backed metadata import path. Code review showed the import selects destination nodes via `metadata_pg_acting_nodes_for_peering_replay` in `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:2390-2403`; that helper only permits `PgState::Peering` in `crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:2869-2878`. Before replay, destination validation calls `validate_metadata_command_replay_state_preserving_pending_slot` for already-imported replicas and `metadata_command_replica_state_can_initialize` for empty replicas in `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:1413-1428`. The Unix server handlers for those calls both invoke `validate_pg_route` first (`crates/storage/src/storage_node_server.rs:7349-7353` and `7379-7388`), but `validate_pg_route` delegates to `validate_pg_route_with_allowed_states(..., &[PgState::Active])` at `crates/storage/src/storage_node_server.rs:8265-8276`; non-allowed states return `InactivePgRoute` at `8354-8358`. I added targeted PoC unit tests that run through the actual UnixStorageNodeClient/StorageNodeServer RPC path. `cargo test -p storage poc_metadata_import_ -- --nocapture` produced: Active route control: `PoC active-route can_initialize result: true`; Peering empty-destination path: `StorageRpc { node_id: 7, operation: "metadata command replica state can initialize", message: "InactivePgRoute: PG 0 route is peering" }`; Peering already-imported/idempotence path: `StorageRpc { node_id: 7, operation: "metadata command validate replay state preserving pending", message: "InactivePgRoute: PG 0 route is peering" }`. I attempted a crash-style run; no process crash occurs because this is a logic/availability failure expressed as an RPC error. Valgrind was attempted but is not installed in the container. LLDB was used non-interactively and stopped at `storage_node_server.rs:8355`; it showed `route->state = Peering`, `allowed_states.length = 1`, and the backtrace `validate_pg_route_with_allowed_states -> validate_pg_route -> metadata_command_replica_state_can_initialize_response -> dispatch_frame`, confirming the exact rejection chain.

